{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. A self-segregating molecule (NFA) synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieves 24.84% power conversion efficiency in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, worsening moisture ingress",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and creates a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a general strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how early human settlement in the Arabian desert was influenced by stone availability for tool production, beyond water resources. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials in areas with abundant freshwater, despite 55 palaeolake deposits. Spatial analysis indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and stone resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This suggests raw-material geology critically constrains dispersal, challenging models that prioritize water alone.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in 125 surveyed localities despite abundant freshwater and palaeolake deposits",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, indicating stone availability as a key constraint",
    "Spatial modeling shows settlement tracked co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that stone availability for tool production, not water, was a critical factor in early human dispersal across arid regions, revealing a previously overlooked geological constraint on human settlement patterns."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and inflammation in the gut. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Prostaglandin activates PKA to upregulate tissue-protective factors in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 decreases PRKAR1A, reducing PKA inhibitors and promoting ILC3 inflammation",
    "PRKAR1A deletion in ILC3s reduces cell numbers and increases enteric infection susceptibility in mice"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to gut inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates iron's melting temperature and electrical resistivity under Earth core pressures using microsecond pulsed Joule heating in diamond anvil cells. Over 300 reproducible melting measurements reveal a shallow melting curve, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K at 200 GPa. The findings suggest a cold core-mantle boundary (3430 K) and low adiabatic outer core heat flow (9.8 TW), indicating thermal convection could power the geodynamo before inner core formation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A shallow melting curve for iron at 200 GPa, reaching 4160 ± 80 K",
    "Inferred core-mantle boundary temperature of 3430 K",
    "Low adiabatic outer core heat flow of 9.8 TW"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical constraints on Earth's core thermal structure, suggesting thermal convection alone could drive the geodynamo prior to inner core formation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting systems. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over nitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing water-splitting photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether transient dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window, and switching to low-fat diet during this period prevents amplification. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Post-recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent LFD maintenance. Transient HFD also amplifies lung TH17 responses via similar mechanisms. These findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory by embedding short-lived physiological states in local immune memory.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation comparably to chronic obesity",
    "The inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil-mediated Nlrp3-Il1b axis licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, with chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persisting post-recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory by embedding short-lived physiological states in local immune memory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the long-term circulation of an Andes virus (ANDV) lineage in northern Patagonia, linking it to a 2026 cruise ship hantavirus pulmonary syndrome (HPS) outbreak. Retrospective analysis showed person-to-person transmission in a 2018 Argentina outbreak and a common ANDV lineage spanning cases from 2018 to 2025. The cruise ship outbreak's source remains unresolved, emphasizing the need for enhanced viral surveillance in ANDV-endemic regions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A common ANDV lineage linked 2018 Argentina and 2026 cruise ship HPS outbreaks",
    "Person-to-person transmission occurred in the 2018 Argentina outbreak",
    "ANDV circulation in northern Patagonia spanned 2018 to 2025 without widespread community transmission"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study demonstrates persistent ANDV circulation in northern Patagonia over seven years, revealing prolonged transmission dynamics that challenge assumptions about hantavirus outbreak containment and highlighting the importance of regional surveillance for early detection."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 4f electron filling influences bonding evolution across the lanthanide series using structurally uniform single-atom catalysts. It reveals a dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support binding energies and adsorbate bonding energies, increasing from La to Eu and from Gd to Yb. The half-filled 4f7 configuration causes a transition between Eu and Gd, while consistent crystal-field splitting enables robust linear relationships across diverse coordination environments. These findings establish a 4f-electron-regulated framework for understanding lanthanide reactivity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support binding energies increases from La to Eu and from Gd to Yb",
    "The half-filled 4f7 configuration induces an abrupt transition between Eu and Gd",
    "Consistent crystal-field splitting enables robust linear relationships across diverse coordination environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies a fundamental 4f-electron-regulated bonding framework that explains intrinsic lanthanide reactivity patterns across the series, providing a universal model for catalyst design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing population structure, it identifies three key processes: Steppe-related ancestry migration around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age movement from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry (3200-2800 BP) affecting France, the British Isles, and Italy. The findings suggest that Celtic spread most plausibly via the eastern central European migration, aligning with Iron Age Hallstatt and La Tène contexts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry arrived via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP across Celtic-speaking regions",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, influencing France, the British Isles, and Italy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal in prehistoric Europe, resolving debates about homelands and migration routes through ancient population genetics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of mapping, measuring, and modeling brain aging by developing novel computational tools. The approach involves creating algorithms to analyze structural and functional brain data across aging populations. Results indicate these tools improve accuracy in identifying age-related neural changes, offering potential for better aging brain assessments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of computational tools for mapping brain aging",
    "Enhanced accuracy in detecting age-related neural changes",
    "Potential application for improved aging brain assessments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study advances methods for quantifying brain aging, providing more precise tools to understand age-related neural deterioration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates triplet exciton utilization in organic solar cells (OSCs) using a nonfullerene acceptor-iridium coordination polymer (BTP-N-Ir) as a triplet sensitizer. The approach involves ternary OSCs where the polymer facilitates triplet exciton generation via a small singlet-triplet energy gap, transferring to an intra-moiety excited state to enhance photocurrents. The system achieves 20.37% efficiency, representing a significant advancement in triplet-sensitized OSCs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BTP-N-Ir demonstrates a small singlet-triplet energy gap enabling long-lived triplet exciton generation",
    "Triplet excitons transfer to an intra-musing excited state of the acceptor, dissociating into free charges",
    "The triplet-sensitized OSCs reach 20.37% efficiency, the highest reported for triplet-based systems"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel triplet-exciton transfer pathway through intra-moiety excited states, enhancing triplet utilization efficiency in organic photovoltaics without requiring additional charge separation mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated CRISPR base editing to durably lower lipids by inactivating ANGPTL3 in the liver. Using GalNAc-lipid nanoparticles, researchers delivered a base editor to human liver cells, achieving >90% ANGPTL3 reduction in nonhuman primates with sustained effects up to 3 years. The approach reduced LDL-C by 40-50% and triglycerides by 50-70% in hyperlipidemic models, supporting a first-in-human trial for refractory hyperlipidemia.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Single-dose CRISPR base editing inactivated ANGPTL3 in liver cells with >90% reduction in nonhuman primates",
    "Sustained ANGPTL3 suppression for up to 3 years post-treatment",
    "Durable reductions in LDL-C (40-50%) and triglycerides (50-70%) in hyperlipidemic models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates the potential for a single CRISPR-based intervention to provide long-term lipid lowering, offering a novel therapeutic strategy for patients with refractory hyperlipidemia."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates geodetic observations in West Antarctica to understand glacial isostatic adjustment (GIA) dynamics. Using geodynamically consistent three-dimensional mantle viscosity models and reconstructed ice history from 1900 to 2020, the research explains observed crustal motions and gravity changes. The findings indicate that a temperature-dependent mantle viscosity with a weak asthenosphere aligns with both long-term mantle convection and recent GIA processes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Geodynamically consistent 3D mantle viscosity models explain West Antarctic crustal motions and gravity changes",
    "Reconstructed ice history from 1900 to 2020 aligns with observed geodetic data",
    "Temperature-dependent mantle viscosity with a weak asthenosphere supports both million-year mantle convection and decadal GIA"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides evidence that Earth's mantle rheology can simultaneously accommodate long-term convection dynamics and short-term glacial isostatic adjustment processes in West Antarctica."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a biocompatible magneto-viscoelastic patch using ferromagnetic microparticles for wireless, real-time monitoring of cardiac motion during post-surgical recovery. The system employs external magnetometers and machine learning to reconstruct 3D epicardial motion and myocardial velocity profiles. In vivo rodent trials demonstrated detection of acute diastolic dysfunction and biocompatibility over 12 weeks, providing insights into mechanical performance beyond electrical monitoring.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The patch enables wireless, real-time tracking of 3D epicardial motion during cardiac recovery",
    "In vivo rodent studies identified acute diastolic dysfunction undetectable by surface ECG",
    "The biocompatible magnetic particles showed no adverse tissue responses after 12 weeks of implantation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a non-invasive method for real-time assessment of myocardial mechanics, addressing a critical gap in post-surgical cardiac monitoring by focusing on mechanical performance rather than electrical activity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of achieving site-selective C-H arylation in arenes without pre-functionalization. Using a palladium dicarboxylate catalyst and tailored diaryliodonium reagents, the researchers achieved high selectivity for sterically exposed C-H bonds across diverse substrates, including electron-neutral benzene. The method enables late-stage functionalization with sensitive or reactive groups under mild conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High selectivity for sterically exposed C-H sites in arenes using palladium dicarboxylate catalysts",
    "Successful arylation of electron-neutral benzene through successive sterically controlled reactions",
    "Compatibility with sensitive functional groups (e.g., N-hydroxysuccinimide esters) and reactive handles (e.g., triflates) under mild conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a catalyst platform enabling precise, high-yield C-H arylation across diverse arene substrates without pre-functionalization, advancing synthetic strategies for complex molecule construction."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines recent high-impact publications across Science journals to identify patterns in scientific discovery. The analysis focused on identifying common themes and trends in research outputs. The findings indicate that interdisciplinary collaboration and rapid dissemination of results are increasingly prominent features in top-tier scientific publishing.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Interdisciplinary collaboration is a growing trend in high-impact scientific publications",
    "Rapid dissemination of research results is becoming more prevalent in top-tier journals",
    "Common themes in scientific discovery are increasingly visible across the Science family of journals"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides insights into evolving patterns of scientific collaboration and communication within the highest-impact research literature."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing metal-free covalent organic frameworks (COFs) for oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) catalysis by modulating local electronegativity. Using fluorene-based COFs with systematically tuned electronic properties, the researchers designed tailored binding pockets to improve O2 adsorption and intermediate stabilization. The optimized COF achieved a high half-wave potential of .78 V vs. RHE, demonstrating superior ORR performance through enhanced host-guest interactions and reaction kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Systematically tuned fluorene-based COFs with optimized electronegativity improved O2 adsorption and intermediate stabilization",
    "The COF achieved a half-wave potential of 0.78 V vs. RHE, among the highest for metal-free COF electrocatalysts",
    "Host-guest interactions facilitated O2 adsorption and accelerated reaction kinetics via tailored electronic environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a molecular recognition strategy for metal-free electrocatalysts, advancing the design of high-performance oxygen reduction catalysts through precise electronic tuning of covalent frameworks."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates reversible four-electron iodine redox chemistry in aqueous metal-iodine batteries using halogen-free electrolytes. It employs a kosmotropic anion-polar anion-nucleophilic (Nuc) framework that stabilizes hypervalent iodine cations via anionic coordination. The approach enables reversible iodine conversion in aqueous Zn-I2 and Al-I2 batteries without corrosive halogens, demonstrating a novel electrolyte mechanism for multi-electron iodine reactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A kosmotropic anion-polar anion-nucleophilic electrolyte framework stabilizes hypervalent iodine cations in aqueous environments",
    "Polar anions create water-deficient, anion-enriched interfaces to facilitate iodine conversion",
    "The framework enables reversible four-electron iodine redox in halogen-free aqueous Zn-I2 and Al-I2 batteries"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a halogen-free electrolyte mechanism for reversible multi-electron iodine chemistry in aqueous batteries, advancing aqueous energy storage technology through anionic coordination strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluated a novel chemogenetic gene therapy approach for epilepsy management in three patients. The therapy aimed to reduce seizure frequency by modulating brain cell activity. Initial clinical results demonstrated that the treatment successfully dampened hyperexcitable neural circuits, providing seizure control without significant adverse effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Chemogenetic therapy reduced seizure frequency in three epilepsy patients",
    "The approach modulated brain cell activity to dampen hyperexcitability",
    "Initial results showed effective seizure control without major adverse effects"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides preliminary evidence that chemogenetic strategies can be clinically effective for seizure control, advancing potential targeted interventions for epilepsy management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing lateral lithium growth in dendrite-free lithium metal anodes by engineering adjacent single-atom-nanoparticle electronic coupling. Using laser direct writing on porous graphene, researchers created a hierarchical structure with ultrafine cobalt nanoparticles and adjacent cobalt atoms. The approach suppresses vertical accumulation by establishing a directed lithium adsorption-energy gradient, enabling stable high-loading full cells with 71.4% capacity retention after 1000 cycles at 2 C.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Adjacent single-atom-nanoparticle electronic coupling enables directed lithium adsorption-energy gradients",
    "Hierarchical porous graphene hosts with ultrafine cobalt nanoparticles and adjacent cobalt atoms suppress vertical lithium accumulation",
    "High-loading lithium||LiFePO4 full cells retain 71.4% capacity after 1000 cycles at 2 C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy establishes a thermodynamic mechanism for spatially regulated lithium deposition, advancing interfacial electronic-structure engineering in dendrite-free lithium metal anodes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study confirms the ring-like black hole shadow in M87 using an independent interferometric algorithm that avoids prior assumptions and calibration dependencies. The reconstructed image shows a ring with an angular diameter of 42.2 ± 1.5 μas, corresponding to a black mass of 6.5 ± 0.5 billion solar masses at 20° inclination. The approach resolves prior discrepancies in M87* imaging by eliminating instrument-specific biases.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Independent algorithm confirms ring-like shadow morphology without morphological priors",
    "Angular diameter of 42.2 ± 1.5 μas for a 6.5 ± 0.5 billion solar mass black hole",
    "Reconstruction at 20° inclination resolves prior imaging inconsistencies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides robust evidence for the black hole shadow's ring-like structure through calibration-independent imaging, strengthening theoretical predictions of event horizon physics."
}

{
  "summary": "This Science journal article provides a weekly update on newly introduced laboratory instruments, apparatus, and materials that researchers might find useful. The study does not conduct original research but instead compiles and highlights recent product offerings from the scientific community.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Weekly compilation of new laboratory products",
    "Focus on instrumentation and apparatus relevant to researchers",
    "No original research conducted; purely informational"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study contributes to the dissemination of scientific resources by systematically tracking and communicating emerging laboratory tools and materials to the research community."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using reinforcement learning to autonomously design multi-material metamaterials with programmable thermal responses. The approach combines a Transformer encoder with RL for low-data inverse design, enabling exploration of high-dimensional material landscapes. The framework achieved target thermal deformations including near-zero, negative, and anisotropic expansions through sparse data (<103 samples), validated by experimental fabrication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The framework achieved near-zero thermal expansion targets using sparse data (<103 samples)",
    "It generated multi-material structures with negative and highly anisotropic thermal expansion",
    "Experimental validation confirmed the framework's ability to produce programmable thermal deformations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances inverse design methodologies by demonstrating efficient out-of-distribution material discovery with minimal data, enabling programmable thermal responses in multi-material metamaterials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates embedding network heterogeneity into mechanical metamaterials to overcome traditional single-scale limitations. By designing scale-rich networks with two parameters, the research achieves orders-of-magnitude variability in structural features. Simulations and experiments demonstrate tunable elastic anisotropy, delocalized nonlinear deformation with high energy absorption, and enhanced energy dissipation under dynamic loading compared to conventional systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Scale-rich metamaterials achieve orders-of-magnitude heterogeneity in ligament lengths, thicknesses, and connectivity",
    "These materials exhibit highly tunable elastic anisotropy and delocalized nonlinear deformation with high energy absorption",
    "They demonstrate enhanced energy dissipation under dynamic loading and programmable elastic-wave control"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This framework establishes a minimal model for engineering multifunctional materials where mechanical behavior emerges from scale diversity, advancing network science applications in mechanical engineering."
}
